# BPMN Diagram Interchange (DI) — Mandatory

Every `.bpmn` file in this repository **must** include a `<bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>` section with coordinates for all shapes and edges. A BPMN file without DI is invisible in the Studio, bpmn.io, and every standards-compliant modeler.

## Rules

- **NEVER** create or modify a `.bpmn` file without a complete `<bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>` section
- **ALWAYS** include `<bpmndi:BPMNShape>` entries for every flow node, data object reference, and lane
- **ALWAYS** include `<bpmndi:BPMNEdge>` entries for every sequence flow
- **ALWAYS** declare the `bpmndi`, `dc`, and `di` namespaces on the `<bpmn:definitions>` element

## Required namespace declarations

```xml
<bpmn:definitions
  xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
  xmlns:bfw="https://bifrostforge.world/schema/bpmn"
  targetNamespace="https://bifrostforge.world/schema/bpmn"
  id="Definitions_1">
```

## Standard element sizes (px)

| Element type | Width | Height |
|---|---|---|
| Start / End / Intermediate / Boundary events | 36 | 36 |
| Tasks (all types), Call Activities | 100 | 80 |
| Gateways (all types) | 50 | 50 |
| Data Object References | 36 | 50 |

## Layout conventions

- **Left-to-right flow.** Start events on the left, end events on the right.
- **Center-line baseline** at approximately `y = 200`.
- **Horizontal spacing** of ~160 px between layer centers.
- **Vertical spacing** of ~100 px between parallel branches.
- **Boundary events** positioned on the bottom border of their host activity (`cy = host.cy + host.height / 2`).
- **Data object references** positioned below the main flow.
- **Lanes** wrap all contained elements with ~30 px padding.
- **Edge waypoints**: straight horizontal line for same-Y connections; three-segment route (horizontal → vertical → horizontal) for connections across different Y levels.

## DI structure

Place the `<bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>` element after the closing `</bpmn:process>` and before `</bpmn:definitions>`. One diagram per process.

```xml
<bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
  <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="your-process-id">
    <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_1" bpmnElement="Start_1">
      <dc:Bounds x="162" y="182" width="36" height="36" />
    </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
    <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_1" bpmnElement="Task_1">
      <dc:Bounds x="290" y="160" width="100" height="80" />
    </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
    <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_1" bpmnElement="End_1">
      <dc:Bounds x="482" y="182" width="36" height="36" />
    </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
    <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_1" bpmnElement="Flow_1">
      <di:waypoint x="198" y="200" />
      <di:waypoint x="290" y="200" />
    </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_Flow_2" bpmnElement="Flow_2">
      <di:waypoint x="390" y="200" />
      <di:waypoint x="482" y="200" />
    </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
  </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
</bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
```

## ID conventions

- Shape IDs: `Shape_<bpmnElementId>` (e.g., `Shape_Start_1`)
- Edge IDs: `Edge_<sequenceFlowId>` (e.g., `Edge_Flow_1`)
- Diagram IDs: `BPMNDiagram_<n>` (1-indexed per process)
- Plane IDs: `BPMNPlane_<n>` (matching diagram index)

## Auto-layout script

If you need to add DI to an existing file that lacks it:

```bash
python3 scripts/bpmn_add_di.py path/to/file.bpmn
```

Files that already contain a `<bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>` are skipped automatically.

## Pool and Lane requirement

Every new BPMN diagram **must** contain at least one pool (`<bpmn:participant>` inside a `<bpmn:collaboration>`) and the process must include a `<bpmn:laneSet>` with a `<bpmn:lane>` named `"default"`. Pool-less diagrams cause serialization issues in the Bifrost Forge World Studio.

## Namespace URI

The canonical `bfw:` namespace URI is `https://bifrostforge.world/schema/bpmn`. Older variants (`http://evilengine.dev/bpmn`, `http://evilengine.io/schema/bpmn`) are deprecated and must not be used in new files.

## Coordinate calculation

For a linear process with `N` elements on a single row:

1. First element center X: `180`, subsequent elements: `+160` per layer
2. All elements center Y: `200`
3. Shape bounds: `x = centerX - width/2`, `y = centerY - height/2`
4. Edge waypoints connect from the right-center of the source to the left-center of the target

For branching (gateway → multiple targets):

1. Targets in the same layer are distributed vertically around the center line (`±100` px spacing)
2. Edge routing uses a midpoint: source-right → midpoint-X at source-Y → midpoint-X at target-Y → target-left